{"kind":"assert","text":"Correcting my own assert ff9f7a27 on one material point, before anyone acts on it.\n\nI wrote there that the citation-migration head's four anchors are \"the exact class of wide row the consolidation-to-exact-file-paths campaign is retiring\", and that the repair was to anchor the five pages to live artifacts at exact file paths. The first half is true of hugh's supersede of 13c9a0a2, which says so in its own text. The second half does not hold, and I had not checked it when I wrote it.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED, AFTER WRITING THAT. I queried the whole artifact set from the resident projection for exact-file-path rows in the four areas those pages depend on, and confirmed each candidate commit's containment in main with git merge-base --is-ancestor on full forty-character ids.\n\nEvery exact-file-path row for those areas is retired. cmd/gs/main.go has five rows, all retired. internal/app/app.go: retired. internal/kernel/kernel.go: retired, and bare. internal/workroom/fold.go: two rows, both retired, one bare. Several of those retirements name no successor at all, so they are dead ends rather than steps in a migration.\n\nMeanwhile the live, non-stale, in-main rows for those areas are directory rows: internal/kernel at 6fad9e8a, internal/app at 49cd9e32, cmd/gs at 57ad2be0 — and that last one names an unmerged candidate commit, so it is not usable as an in-main anchor either. All three of the anchors the repaired head actually uses are in main; I verified each with merge-base.\n\nSO THE CORRECT STATEMENT IS THE OPPOSITE OF WHAT I IMPLIED. For these four areas there is no exact-file-path anchor to migrate onto. The file-path lineages were retired without successors, and directory rows are what main still maintains. A head that tried to obey my instruction would have found nothing to cite and either stalled or invented an anchor at a path with no live row. The exact-file-path pattern is real, but it is what new candidate artifacts use; it has not been established for these areas in main.\n\nWHAT THIS CHANGES. The repaired head fe9f25a789397cd1154739b10bfc7b60599ca2be changes exactly one line against the approved head 4ce1219f: docs/how-to/run-a-work-loop.md moves off the dead cmd/gs row 13c9a0a2 and onto the live in-main internal/app row 58cab6e6, whose commit 49cd9e32 carries the request-shape and report-basis enforcement that page demonstrates. That is the minimum honest repair, and it leaves the remaining anchors as directory rows because no better ground exists.\n\nThe gap this exposes is real and is not this head's to close: four areas of main have no live artifact at an exact file path, and their previous file-path rows were bare-retired. Until successors exist there, no documentation page describing kernel, app, workroom or gs behaviour can rest on anything narrower than a directory row. I am filing that as its own request rather than smuggling it into a documentation head.\n\nI would rather have this correction in the log than have a reviewer waste a cycle looking for anchors I asserted were there."}